<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Only bread and only wine,</l><l>Yet to faith, the solemn sign</l><l>Of the heav’nly and divine!</l><l>We give Thee thanks, O Lord.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>For the words that turn our eye</l><l>To the cross of Calvary,</l><l>Bidding us in faith draw nigh,</l><l>We give Thee thanks, O Lord.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>For the words that fragrance breathe</l><l>These plain symbols underneath,</l><l>Words that His own peace bequeath,</l><l>We give Thee thanks, O Lord.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>For Thy words in Spirit, shown,</l><l>For Thy will to us made known,</l><l>“Do ye this until I come,”</l><l>We give Thee thanks, O Lord.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>Till He come we take the bread,</l><l>Type of Him on whom we feed,</l><l>Him who liveth and was dead!</l><l>We give Thee thanks, O Lord.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>Till He come we take the cup;</l><l>As we at His table sup,</l><l>Eye and heart are lifted up!</l><l>We give Thee thanks, O Lord.</l></lg>
<lg label="8."><l>For that coming, here foreshown,</l><l>For that day to man unknown,</l><l>For the glory and the throne,</l><l>We give Thee thanks, O Lord.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
